in sys/arch/alpha/tc/scc.c I find the following code which suggests it
should be possible to restart from DDB:

	/* Break on serial console drops into the debugger */
	if ((value & ZSRR0_BREAK) && CONSOLE_ON_UNIT(sc->sc_dv.dv_unit)) {
#ifdef DDB
		splx(s);		/* spl0()? */
		Debugger();
		return;
#else
		/* XXX maybe fall back to PROM?  DEFINITELY!!!! */
#endif
	}


My AS4000 uses the com driver for the serial console of course.  

	com0 at isa0 port 0x3f8-0x3ff irq 4: ns16550a, working fifo
	com0: console

The system seems to have the default setup so that a true RS232 BREAK
should be recognized as the signal to go to DDB:

	hw.cnmagic = '^A
	machdep.console_device = ttyC0
	ddb.fromconsole = 1

Ah!  I can get to the debugger with a custom magic break sequence!

